      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If I really wanted things to stick to my hand, I'd change the grab binding in SteamVR to a \"Toggle\" type thing. I don't, though, and some random pickups getting stuck to my hand makes me think that the grip capsense finally died. It's mildly infuriating. \n\nNo other VR game that I can remember does this for grab-type interactions. The closest I can think of is weapons in Alyx, but those are explicitly equipped, not grabbed. The way VRC does it is simply inconsistent - I never know if a pickup is normal, or this sticky garbage.\n\nUdon already can do the \"equip\" type thing (just move the object to the hand bone each frame), so this \"feature\" seems absolutely unnecessary and counter-productive. *Especially* if someone had the bright idea to annoy world makers into enabling this by default, as other comments imply.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "698bab7c4229f2bdf866a31c",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f3477471c7a477bc948affb",
        "alias": "Khaki Piranha",
        "aliasID": "65c29afded6eefce4c55ea73",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/1be430face99759a37e4e702919f98b9.png",
        "created": "2020-08-12T23:12:07.034Z",
        "name": "Sharrnah",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-02-10T22:04:44.194Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "68c491f50f703a7bf06abcff",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Please VRChat make this optional TO THE USER.\n\nHow can a World creator decide how things are hold if they don't even know the type of controller the user has?\n\nOr is it expected that World Creators first ask the player what type of controller and then decide for this?\n\nThis is really annoying.\n\nLuckily most worlds so far i encountered only used this sparingly or reverted it back completely.\n\nBut even then it was always a surprise that it got stuck to my hand without notice and with no obvious way to get rid of it again until you remember \"Ah that stupid auto-hold again\".\n\nThe only controller i can think of where it _might_ make sense is the Vive Wand Controller. All others have a more \"natural\" type of grabbing things by closing the hand (You know, like in reality you do it too without stuff suddenly sticking to your hand even when opening the hand again).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
