        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Many of worlds which use auto-hold feature in them still seem not to have switch to disable it (I should note that I haven't confirmed whether this feature can be en/disabled on runtime).\n\nAs some game worlds require accurate control for pickups, Being forced to deal with auto-hold keeps me from immersive and comfortable experience. I can't remember \"will it leave off my hand if I release grip trigger next time?\" for every single action.\n\nTypical VR controller takes grip action as continuous one and actually I grip it, so auto-hold is not intuitive. It's for click-and-toggle style inputs.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-09-12T21:34:45.386Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For how much I like auto-hold being available for accessibility, I really hope that it can be toggled off in the settings for VR users. As someone who really hates \"sticky pickups\" in VR games; this is a must for me. Having pickups stick to my hand until I press the grip button again is very unintuitive for me and doesn't feel natural whatsoever",
